// moon-fuzz coverage.
//
// Two feedback sources, both behind the same idea of "a signature the engine
// can compare":
//
//   recorder — manual instrumentation (`@cov.hit(id)` at branches the target
//              author chose). Exact, per execution, works on every backend.
//              This is what instrumented targets get.
//
//   buckets  — no instrumentation needed: a signature derived from the output
//              shape. Weak, but it is what an uninstrumented target gets, so
//              `moonx fuzz run` never requires the user to touch their code.
//
// The compiler's own coverage artifacts are parsed in `edges.mbt`; they are a
// test-run feature and are not wired into the engine (see the architecture doc).
import {
  "QYF795/moonsting/core",
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8",
}
